# Pinned 2026-10-02 by panel 187's compiler engineer, route (1f): a known
# cost, not an intent; a change in either direction turns this case red.
# C's do-while in a braced body: the inner braces are passed and the
# function's braces passed whole after its lines are read
# (`parse/braced_lines.hero:154`, `brace_habit.pass`), and what follows the
# inner `}` on its line is not read. Row 131-32: `while (1 == 1)` is told
# only once the braces are gone. Class (b): `adjacent`.
#
# Moved 2026-10-04 with defect 201's repair (lane b9-recovery): the line past
# the inner `}` is read, the tail's own mistakes told, and what was hidden is
# the do-while itself, which no word here writes: the `do {`'s `{` is told as
# that habit, with the loop that replaces it
# (`parse/loop_habit.past_a_statement`); it pins that now.

function main() {  #~ missing_body
    do {  #~ expected_end_of_line
        y = 3 4  #~ expected_end_of_line
    } while (1 == 1)
}
